/ "if <file> exists" must ask file.exists and branch on ITS result, not test whatever the previous step
/ left in %!data%. A data-leaving step first makes %!data% truthy, so the old shape
/ (condition.if(Left=%!data%)) would fire for a missing file too. An existing file must fire, a missing one
/ must not — the missing-file branch is the discriminator.
Start
- write out "something before"
- save "hi" to file 'here.json'
- if 'here.json' exists, set %seen% = true
- if 'gone.json' exists, set %missing% = true
- assert %seen% is true
- assert %missing% is empty
